          "snippet": "Optical trapping has been used in various research fields including biology [4,5], biochemistry [6,7], materials engineering and nanofabrication [8], atomic physics [9], photonic force microscopy [10] etc. These and other applications are discussed in a number of reviews devoted to optical trapping [8,[11][12][13].",
